      fix: parse generic method invocation with single type argument (#103) (#104)
      
      * fix: parse generic method invocation with single type argument (#103)
      
      `selector.field<int>(parametr)` was parsed as two nested
      relational_expression nodes — `(selector.field < int) > (parametr)` —
      instead of a generic method invocation. This is the classic Dart
      `a.b<c>(d)` ambiguity: it only surfaced for a single type argument plus
      non-empty parenthesized args, since multiple type args (comma) or empty
      `()` already made the relational reading invalid.
      
      Give `argument_part` a positive `prec.dynamic` so the GLR parser prefers
      the `type_arguments arguments` reading over relational_expression for the
      `[$.type_arguments, $.relational_operator]` conflict, matching how Dart
      itself resolves it. Genuine relational expressions are unaffected.
      
